Tonight I achieved my goal of ascending every role on NAO. My journey
started with a priestess in January and ended with a Samurai in
August. I was determined not to let this Samurai meet the fate of the
last, ill from Pestilence and battered down mere steps from the high
altar.

I had a hard time getting going as I couldn't find early sources of
either magic resistance or reflection. Unwilling to do the quest or
Ludios (which appeared at a quite early level in this game) without
them, I eventually had what I thought was a clever idea. I had already
blown my usual no-polyself conduct by stepping on a polytrap, and in
the meantime had come upon a ring of polymorph control. So I became a
gray dragon and laid some eggs (one of the main reasons I always play
female characters, just in case!). It took forever to raise my babies
to adulthood, and in fact all but one died before maturing. The final
one I fed to a fire elemental, and, what do you know, no scales. Back
to the drawing board. Eventually I was able to rev-geno more gray
dragons and get scales that way.

With magic resistance I felt confident enough to go for the castle,
and wished for an amulet of reflection there. I could then go back and
do the quest (wand of death - easy), Ludios, etc. with confidence. A
number of altars had appeared before this time, including a cross-
aligned temple, which helped in gaining protection without having to
go all the way back to Minetown. I got Frost Brand but gave up on
waiting for Grayswandir, and settled for Frosty plus my original
katana (enchanted +7/+6 respectively). I figured the katana did more
damage than a saber other than the silver damage, and while two-
weaponing would allow me to use both weapons at expert skill.

I found many scrolls of genocide and so eliminated L h ; , my usual
set when not playing no-gen conduct, and disenchanters. Wanted to
bribe Asmodeus but dropped and forgot my change; he disappeared for
awhile, digging down whenever I got close. Did bribe Baalzebub. Didn't
manage to kill Orcus before he depleted his wand of death, but I'd
already found many more (and not just in the quest), helpful when
Rodney reappeared twice before I even made it out of the Sanctum.
Found a spellbook of charm monster and managed to charm a couple of
purple worms at one point, though one turned into an iron golem (not
bad, till he fell through a hole) and another died somewhere on the
way back up.

When I found a cloak of magic resistance in Gehennom I decided to rev-
geno silver dragons and change my armor. I was gunshy after the last
oh-so-close Samurai attempt, and wanted to wear an amulet of life
saving instead of reflection. Fortunately I didn't need it; the first
altar visited on Astral was the right one, and I offered for my 14th
ascension, 13th and final NAO class. Whew! Time for a Nethack
vacation...

